# Tokens in components (`@refineui/react`)

In Figma the flow is **Foundation → Web Kit**. Color·padding·spacing·radius are tied to Foundation; in code reference them only via `@refineui/tokens`.

Component **scope and variants** must match **Web Kit Figma** — see `figma-foundation` rule.

## MUST
- **Color·spacing·radius·stroke·typography·shadow·z-index** come only from `@refineui/tokens`.
- **Foundation `Global/Size/{n}` scale** is referenced only via **`foundationSizes`** in `@refineui/react`.
- **Per–Web Kit component dimensions** come only from **`componentSizes`**. **Icon glyph pixels** use **`iconSizes`** from `@refineui/tokens`; **modal scrim** uses `overlays`.
- **No hardcoding**: no arbitrary `px`, `#hex`, or `rgb()` in component styles. (Exceptions: literal `0`, `minWidth: 0`.)
- When new dimensions are needed, add them to `foundationSizes` or `componentSizes` per Figma spec first.

## RECOMMENDED
- In documentation Previews, prefer the same tokens and semantic colors.